guide forever/40-50/shendralas
title Shen'dralas
levels 45-46 Alliance
levels 46-47 Horde
zone Shen'dralas
coords live
why About a dozen quests on a short trip into Forever's new zone (about 45-46 for the Alliance, 47 for the Horde), then on to Feralas.
keywords shen'dralas, shendralas, valley of bones, evenshade's overlook, forlorn gardens, bristleback retreat, pylons, desolace
next forever/horde/40-50/03-feralas
next forever/alliance/40-50/03-feralas

# Shen'dralas for both factions (2026-11-12, in both routes since 0.4.0). Hand-written from players' recordings of
# the zone (99 sessions, 56 people, most of them passing through below level 40), with Forever's quest data for
# titles, levels and objectives and the client's tables for item and spell names. Its quests are 41-45; on both
# routes it comes at the levels the header gives each side. Horde: the route since 0.4.0, after the Feralas & Tanaris guide (40-50/02, Camp Mojache,
# about level 46 with the Riverglades before it); in by the ride north from Camp Mojache into Desolace's south (a
# fresh starter flies to Shadowprey Village), out by the flight from Shadowprey (or the hearth to Camp Mojache) to
# Orgrimmar, where the next Feralas guide starts with Orgrimmar's hand-ins. Alliance: the route since 0.4.0, after the
# Badlands guide (40-50/02, Theramore, about level 45 with the Riverglades before it); in from Nijel's Point, out on
# the ride south into Feralas, where the Feralas guide picks up at the Feathermoon boat.
# Order: the Tattered Journal from the valley's necromancers; Mordent Evenshade's pylons (find the three, the
# fragment and the shard in Desolace's two centaur villages, the Mana Sieve and the repairs, his story, then
# Magister Kirandis in the temple); the temple's own quests once Kirandis has been met; Mithera's Forlorn Gardens.
# Offered only after another quest is handed in (players' recordings, one player each, so leads to confirm):
# Fragments of the Pylons after Strange Pylons; Powering the Pylons after Fragments of the Pylons; A Brief History
# Lesson after Powering the Pylons; Meeting the Magister after A Brief History Lesson; What They've Done to My
# Peonies and Word of the Woods after Forlorn Gardens. Mithera was only recorded after Meeting the Magister was
# handed in, so the temple's quests wait for it here.
# Left out on purpose:
# - The Gelkis and Magram quests of the Valley of Bones (Nerlokh, Orgrul, Hagiak, Rokren; Valley of Bones,
#   Khan Jehn and the rest): each asks for Honored with its centaur clan (forever/reputation/centaur-clans).
# - Vindael's Phantasmal Problems (93450), Spectral Iron Ore (93546) and Tempered Expectations (96060): nobody
#   recorded them, and the data places none of the spectral ore deposits.
# - Mana Mania (99258): its Nascent Pylon Protector is an elite (level 43), and nobody recorded it.
# - Rot and Regret (93404, Maraudon), Passing the Blame (93601) after it, Agamaggan's Blood (93604, Razorfen Downs)
#   and Not on Squealing Terms (93606): dungeon quests and their follow-ups; Kog'thug the Brave, who gives the last
#   two, was hostile to every player who met him.
# - Corpsefeeder's Carapace (93574, from an elite) and Forlorn Necklace (93609, no known source).

step North into Desolace
  only Horde
  when zone "Feralas"
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in Shen'dralas. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Shen'dralas lies south of Desolace, through the Valley of Bones, and has no flight path of its own. From Camp Mojache ride north-west on the road past Dire Maul and on north into Desolace: the road comes out on Desolace's southern edge.
  goto 43.0,96.0 map 1443 "Desolace, where the road from Feralas comes in"

step Fly to Shadowprey Village
  only Horde
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  when !zone "Desolace"
  when !zone "Feralas"
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in Shen'dralas. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Shen'dralas lies south of Desolace, through the Valley of Bones, and has no flight path of its own. Its quests are for levels 41-45. Coming from the Eastern Kingdoms, take the zeppelin to Orgrimmar first (from Grom'gol or the Undercity).
  zone Orgrimmar
  goto 45.3,63.7 "Orgrimmar flight master"
  fly "Shadowprey Village"
  zone Desolace

step Fly to Nijel's Point
  only Alliance
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  when !zone "Desolace"
  tip New in Forever: this guide follows what players did in Shen'dralas. If a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip Shen'dralas lies south of Desolace, through the Valley of Bones, and has no flight path of its own. Its quests are for levels 41-45. Coming from the Eastern Kingdoms, take the boat from Menethil Harbor to Theramore first.
  fly "Nijel's Point"

step Into the Valley of Bones
  only Horde
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip Ride east along Desolace's southern edge (from Shadowprey Village: past Gelkis Village): the Valley of Bones opens there into Shen'dralas.
  enter "Shen'dralas" @21.2,22.4

step Into the Valley of Bones
  only Alliance
  when !zone "Shen'dralas"
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip Ride south from Nijel's Point down the road through eastern Desolace to Magram Village: just past its western edge the path climbs into the Valley of Bones and Shen'dralas.
  enter "Shen'dralas" @33.0,5.8

step The Valley of Bones: a Tattered Journal
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip New in Forever: if a step is wrong, tell us on Polestar's Discord or GitHub and name the step.
  tip The Outcast Necromancers and the Magram Necromancers of the valley drop a Tattered Journal whose writer lives in Shen'dralas: players got it within a few kills. The Magram centaurs leave you be until you attack; the Magram Necrokhans among them (level 45) are elites: leave them be.
  tip The Gelkis and Magram centaurs have Valley of Bones quest chains of their own, worth about 20,000 to 30,000 more experience, but each chain asks for Honored with its clan. The two clans are rivals, so work for one of them: the Gelkis and Magram Centaur Reputation guide, under Reputation, shows how.
  collect 260347
  accept 93644

step The western pylon
  tip East through the valley to the strange crystal on its pedestal: clicking it starts Strange Pylons. The Decrepit Pylon Protectors (levels 42-43) around it are the mana elementals that guard it. Corpsefeeders (level 45, elite) roam the valley east of here.
  accept 92914 object 577959

step Bristleback Retreat: the eastern pylon
  tip East along the valley road to the quilboar of Bristleback Retreat: the second pylon stands at the eastern end of their camp. A Corpsefeeder (level 45, elite) walks this road: let it pass. The Bristlebacks (levels 42-43) attack on sight; Kog'thug the Brave (level 43, elite) and his bodyguards hold the south side of the camp.
  goto 73.2,23.2 "the eastern pylon" r 15

step The temple of Shen'dralas: the third pylon
  tip South to the Shen'dralar temple at the zone's heart, keeping west of Kog'thug's bodyguards: the third pylon stands inside. The temple's guards are neutral: leave them be.
  complete 92914 @47.6,76.7

step Evenshade's Overlook
  tip North-west from the temple to Mordent Evenshade's camp on the overlook, beside the spirit healer: the Tattered Journal is his, and he wants to hear about the pylons.
  turnin 93644
  turnin 92914
  accept 96010

step North into Desolace
  zone Desolace
  tip Mordent wants a fragment and a shard of the pylons back from Desolace's two centaur villages: Magram Village lies just beyond the valley's northern way out.
  tip Careful: if you have killed Magram or Gelkis centaurs, that clan's guards may attack you when you walk into its village.
  enter "Desolace" @64.0,80.4

step Magram Village
  zone Desolace
  tip The Pylon Fragment lies at the western edge of the village; Magram Guardians (levels 39-41) watch over it.
  collect 255656 x1 quest 96010.1 @68.1,79.2

step Gelkis Village
  zone Desolace
  tip West along Desolace's southern edge to Gelkis Village: the Pylon Shard lies at its southern end, watched by Gelkis Guardians (levels 39-41).
  collect 255657 x1 quest 96010.2 @36.1,85.6

step Back into the Valley of Bones
  zone Shen'dralas
  tip East again along Desolace's southern edge: the Valley of Bones opens into Shen'dralas.
  enter "Shen'dralas" @21.2,22.4

step Evenshade's Overlook
  turnin 96010
  accept 96018

step The temple: the Mana Sieve
  when onquest 96018
  when !complete 96018
  tip Mordent sends you for the Mana Sieve, kept inside the temple beside Historian Biraxas. Powering the Pylons asks you to gather mana with the Sieve before you repair the pylons: with it in your bags you can handle the Unstable Mana Rifts, the floating sparks of mana all along the road north.
  collect 255662 @45.9,78.2

step Four crystals for the first unfinished pylon
  label first-pylon-crystals
  when onquest 96018
  when !complete 96018
  tip Use the Mana Sieve on Unstable Mana Rifts north of the temple. Each repair spends four crystals. If both pylons are unfinished, gather eight here or refill on the valley road after the western repair. If only one is unfinished, four are enough. Let the wandering elite Protectors pass.
  use 255662 optional @40.18,49.62 -- Mana Sieve on an Unstable Mana Rift
  collect 255667 x4 @40.18,49.62 -- Coalesced Mana Crystals for one repair

step The road south of the western pylon
  label western-pylon-approach
  when done first-pylon-crystals
  when !complete 96018
  tip Check the western repair in your quest log. If it is already checked, do not visit this waypoint: take four crystals east to Bristleback Retreat (73.4,23.9). Enter from the west and stay off the south side, away from Kog'thug and his bodyguards. Repair the eastern pylon there; the route resumes when the log shows both.
  tip North up the road to the first pylon, gathering mana from the Unstable Mana Rifts on the way. Stop where the arrow points, on the road just south of the pylon, keeping to its west edge: the quiet side, with no Protectors behind you. Pull one Decrepit Pylon Protector at a time down to that spot, the one nearest the pylon's south side first, and kill it there; then step up to the pylon's west side and use Repair and Recharge Pylon, as players did to repair it.
  tip Careful: stay off the pylon's east and north-east side. The Protectors stand there two and three together, a Corpsefeeder (level 45, elite) walks among them and the Magram Necrokhans (elites, 45) stand just beyond: nearly every recorded death at this pylon happened east of it. If the Magram attack you (they do once you have killed Magram), wait at the arrow until any Necrokhan by the pylon walks off before you pull. Nascent Pylon Protectors (elites, 43) wander the road south of it: let them pass.
  tip If you die here, walk your ghost back to the arrow before you come back to life: players who rose beside the pylon died again within seconds.
  goto 43.9,37.0 "the road just south of the western pylon" r 10

step The western pylon: repair it
  label western-pylon-repaired
  when done western-pylon-approach
  loop
  goto 43.97,35.59 r 4
  goto 43.89,35.64 r 4
  tip Pull one Decrepit Pylon Protector back to the road if it guards the crystal. Stand on the west face and use Repair and Recharge Pylon. The quest log must show the western pylon repaired; a dead Protector alone does not count.
  cast 1289727 "Repair and Recharge Pylon" optional @43.97,35.59
  interact 577959 quest 96018.2 -- Repair the western pylon from this side

step Four crystals for the eastern pylon
  label eastern-pylon-crystals
  when done western-pylon-repaired
  when onquest 96018
  when !complete 96018
  tip Check your bags after the western repair. If fewer than four crystals remain, use the Sieve on rifts along the valley road before entering Bristleback Retreat. Give roaming Corpsefeeders and hostile Necrokhans room.
  use 255662 optional @51.60,36.94 -- Mana Sieve on an Unstable Mana Rift
  collect 255667 x4 @51.60,36.94 -- Four unspent Coalesced Mana Crystals

step Bristleback Retreat: repair the eastern pylon
  when done eastern-pylon-crystals
  tip Enter from the west. Pull a single Decrepit Pylon Protector clear if needed, then use Repair and Recharge Pylon at the eastern crystal. Keep away from Kog'thug the Brave and his bodyguards on the south side of the camp.
  cast 1289727 "Repair and Recharge Pylon" optional @73.4,23.91
  interact 577960 quest 96018.3 @73.4,23.91 -- Repair the eastern pylon, then return to Mordent

step Unfinished pylon repairs
  when onquest 96018
  when !complete 96018
  tip Check your quest log before going back to Mordent. Each unchecked pylon needs four crystals from the rifts. For the western repair, approach from the road at 43.9,37.0 and use the west face. For the eastern repair, enter Bristleback Retreat from the west. Return to Mordent only after both repairs count.
  tip If you want to leave Shen'dralas now, keep the quest. This line takes you back to your Feralas route; you can return for the unfinished repair later.
  task "Leave Shen'dralas with the repair quest in my log"

step Evenshade's Overlook
  when complete 96018
  tip Follow the valley road west and south to Mordent with both repairs finished.
  turnin 96018

step A Brief History Lesson
  when turnedin 96018
  tip Hear Mordent out, then speak to him again for the reward.
  accept 93016
  talk 253471 quest 93016.1           -- Mordent Evenshade: hear him out
  turnin 93016

step Meeting the Magister
  when turnedin 93016
  accept 93394

# Liranne is not there before Mordent's pylons chain is done (#2946: she was missing for a player who had only found
# the pylons, so While you're here sent the collar to an empty spot): the step waits for A Brief History Lesson.
step Liranne
  when has 259461
  when turnedin 93016
  tip A Prowler gave up a Partially Digested Collar: Liranne, north of the temple, knows whose it was.
  accept 93568
  turnin 93568

step The temple: Magister Kirandis
  when turnedin 93016
  tip Magister Kirandis waits inside the temple. Then Mithera, on the temple's eastern side, has work in the Forlorn Gardens.
  turnin 93394
  accept 93341

step The Forlorn Gardens: the pedestal
  when onquest 93341
  tip East of the temple the Forlorn Gardens have run wild, and their plants attack on sight. Examine the pedestal at the gardens' southern end.
  complete 93341 @70.3,79.7

step Mithera
  when complete 93341
  turnin 93341

step Mithera’s garden errands
  when turnedin 93341
  accept 93362
  accept 93594

step The Forlorn Gardens
  when turnedin 93341
  tip Rowdy Roses and Terrible Tulips grow all over the gardens; the Malevolent Marigolds keep to the northern part. Woodwyrd, the treant in the middle of the gardens, has a request of his own that needs water from Maraudon, a dungeon: this guide leaves it.
  tip The Shen'dralar who wander the gardens are neutral, like the temple's guards: leave them be and pull the flowers away from them. Careful: Nascent Pylon Protectors (elites, 43) wander the zone's middle, the gardens too: keep clear of them.
  kill 254566 x4 quest 93362.1        -- Rowdy Rose
  kill 254567 x4 quest 93362.2        -- Terrible Tulip
  kill 254572 x20 quest 93362.3       -- Malevolent Marigold
  turnin 93594

step Mithera
  when complete 93362
  turnin 93362

step The temple: Historian Biraxas
  when turnedin 93394
  tip Historian Biraxas, inside the temple, has a task for you now that you have met Magister Kirandis: the heart of a Decrepit Pylon Protector (42-43, not elite), a short ride back up the road north.
  accept 99257                        -- Historian Biraxas

step A Heart of Crystal
  when onquest 99257
  tip The nearest Decrepit Pylon Protectors stand by the road north, from the middle of the zone up to the western pylon, and around Mordent's overlook: one of them carries the heart Biraxas wants.
  collect 286647 quest 99257.1

step Historian Biraxas
  when complete 99257
  tip Shen'dralas is done: ride back north through the Valley of Bones; the next step says where your route goes on from there.
  turnin 99257

step Shadowprey Village
  only Horde
  zone Desolace
  tip Shen'dralas is done. Ride back north through the Valley of Bones and west along Desolace's southern edge to Shadowprey Village: the next guide picks up in Orgrimmar, with the Feralas guide's hand-ins. Your hearthstone is bound at Camp Mojache: if it is ready, hearth there and fly to Orgrimmar from Camp Mojache instead.
  goto 21.56,74.04 "Shadowprey Village flight master"
  fly "Orgrimmar"
  zone Orgrimmar

step Back to your route
  only Alliance
  note Shen'dralas is done. Your Feralas guide picks up from here: ride back north through the Valley of Bones, west along Desolace's southern edge and south into Feralas, to the dock on the Forgotten Coast where the boat crosses to Feathermoon Stronghold.
